			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1789889675854,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "• A single infinite sheet gives |E| = σ/(2ε₀). That's why option A is a trap!\n• A polarized slab has TWO opposite sheets (+P top, -P bottom) like a capacitor.\n• Outside: fields point in opposite directions and exactly CANCEL to 0.",
			"fontSize": 14,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "• A single infinite sheet gives |E| = σ/(2ε₀). That's why option A is a trap!\n• A polarized slab has TWO opposite sheets (+P top, -P bottom) like a capacitor.\n• Outside: fields point in opposite directions and exactly CANCEL to 0.",
